    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664-a1">

                <pb facs="1064" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg928"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 212.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Légitime to Mr.
                            Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Relations, Section No.</hi>
                                ——,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-10-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 13, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to bring to your
                    knowledge that on account of the recent taking up of arms that has taken place
                    at St. Marc and at Gonaïves, the provisional government has judged it
                    indispensable to authorize the bombardment of those two rebel cities.</p>
                <p>I beg you, in consequence, to have the kindness to take the necessary measures
                    for the preservation of your fellow-citizens from the evils that may result from
                    this urgent decision.</p>
                <p>The two ships of war of the Government will leave forthwith this night.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. D.
                            Légitime.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
